    "narrative": "The core of our lineup today rests on the dynamic upside of **Corbin Carroll** (85.94) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs above 4.30. **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, leveraging a massive +19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s inefficiency and a +10% order bonus, setting him up as the primary engine for our 5x5 categories. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime spot; he receives a significant +14% park factor boost and a +14% platoon advantage, making him a high-efficiency start. **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.15) round out our top-tier tier, capitalizing on weak opposing pitching to provide the floor we need to remain competitive in Roto.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the rotation today was leaving **Zach McKinstry** on the bench with a score of 38.04. While he offers some utility, his deep batting order position (#9) and unfavorable park factors significantly dampened his outlook compared to the rest of the roster. Ultimately, **Travis Bazzana** (40.27) held onto the MI slot due to his higher base potential, despite a tough matchup against Manaea. Managers must remain vigilant regarding **Austin Riley** (57.44); while he has a solid matchup against Ryan Gusto, he is tagged with a 44% rain risk, which could shorten his day and cap his production. We are also monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Cole Young**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **James Wood**, all of whom are currently listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have projected their positions, any last-minute defensive swaps could impact our scoring efficiency. \n\nBeyond our active starters, the remainder of the organization continues to be managed with strict oversight. We are holding **Jose Caballero**, **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** in reserve, with the IL status of **Trevor Story** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** keeping them strictly off-limits for active play. We are pushing for maximum efficiency today, banking on the speed and situational advantages of **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood** to bridge our gap in the stolen base category.",
